### 2. Collapsible Description (Read More / Read Less)
We need to introduce a state to toggle the description text. Since SelectedVoucherCard in VoucherPosting is a functional variable inside the main component, it's better to extract it slightly or just use a local state.
**In VoucherPosting (Update SelectedVoucherCard):**
```javascript
const SelectedVoucherCard = () => {
  // 1. Add local state for this card
  const [isDescExpanded, setIsDescExpanded] = useState(false);
  
  if (!selectedVoucher) return null;

  const desc = selectedVoucher.description || "No description provided.";
  const isLongDesc = desc.length > 100; // Adjust threshold as needed

  return (
    <Paper elevation={0} sx={jpStyles.svPaper}>
      {/* ... Header and Grid Setup ... */}
      
        <Grid item size={12}>
          <Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary" display="block" gutterBottom>Description</Typography>
          <Typography variant="body2" sx={{ whiteSpace: "pre-wrap", lineHeight: 1.6, fontWeight: 300 }}>
            {isLongDesc && !isDescExpanded ? `${desc.substring(0, 100)}...` : desc}
            {isLongDesc && (
              <Typography 
                component="span" 
                color="primary" 
                onClick={() => setIsDescExpanded(!isDescExpanded)}
                sx={{ cursor: "pointer", ml: 1, fontWeight: "bold", '&:hover': { textDecoration: 'underline' } }}
              >
                {isDescExpanded ? "Read Less" : "Read More"}
              </Typography>
            )}
          </Typography>
        </Grid>
      </Grid>
    </Paper>
  );
};

```
