### 3. Fixing Autocomplete noOptionsText and History
To prevent MUI Autocomplete from caching and displaying old search results when the input length is less than 3, we must dynamically override the options array to be empty [] when the condition isn't met.
Update the Autocomplete properties for **both Branch and CGL** in VoucherPosting:
**For Branch Autocomplete:**
```javascript
<Autocomplete
  // ... other props
  options={
    // FORCE options to empty if input is less than 3 characters
    (branchInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3
      ? [] 
      : (row.branch && !branchSearch.options.some((o) => o.code === row.branch.code)
          ? [row.branch, ...branchSearch.options]
          : branchSearch.options)
  }
  noOptionsText={
    (branchInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 
      ? "Min 3 Digits Required Search" 
      : "No branches found"
  }
  // ... rest of your Autocomplete setup
/>

```
**For CGL Autocomplete:**
```javascript
<Autocomplete
  // ... other props
  options={
    // FORCE options to empty if input is less than 3 characters
    (cglInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3
      ? []
      : (row.cgl && !cglSearch.options.some((o) => o.cglNumber === row.cgl.cglNumber)
          ? [row.cgl, ...cglSearch.options]
          : cglSearch.options)
  }
  noOptionsText={
    (cglInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 
      ? "Min 3 Digits Required Search" 
      : "No CGL found"
  }
  // ... rest of your Autocomplete setup
/>

```
By explicitly evaluating (branchInputValues[row.id] || "").length < 3 ? [] : ... within the options prop itself, React and MUI are forced to drop the old cached options the moment the user clears out the input field or drops below the 3-character threshold, elegantly resolving the history bug.
